 Hello,




 



 We are updating Ubisoft’s 
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Terms of Use  and 
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/privacypolicy/ 
Privacy Policy . 
Below is a recap of the key changes. If you wish to learn more about the update, please 
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/update 
check this page .







 
 



 













 






 Among other updates, the Privacy Policy will be updated to:
	- Make it easier to understand what data we collect and how we use it
	- Provide improved guidance on how you can exercise your rights over your personal data in the Privacy Center
	- Give you information about how your data is handled for new features and services


 



 












 




 



 We have also introduced additional resources, 
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/privacypolicyminors/ 
including a Privacy Policy for Young Players , and a 
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/privacy/ 
Guide to your personal data , intended to help you better understand and manage how your personal data is used.




 
 












 



 


 Among other updates, the Terms of Use will be updated to:

	- Detail the protective measures and parental controls available (Family Settings) for Ubisoft accounts (
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Article 3 ) and our player safety policies (
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Article 7 )
	- Give additional information about updates and changes we may make to digital content and services, and applicable warranties (
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Article 5  and 
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Article 10 )
	- Provide more information about our obligation to delete inactive accounts (
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Article 8 )

	- Update our arbitration agreement for US residents (
https://www.ubisoft.com/legal/documents/termsofuse 
Article 16 )

With this update, we wanted to provide all users with a unique and worldwide version of the Terms of Use. This may result in changes to numbering or paragraphs compared to your current version. Where needed, we specified if a given article of paragraph applies to residents of specific countries.


 

 
 












 




 



 You will have until  March 20, 2026 to accept the updated Terms of Use. They will become effective for you and all our users on such date, unless you accept them earlier.


If you do not agree to these changes, you can request the closure of your Ubisoft account on the 
https://account.ubisoft.com/account-information 
Account Management Page .


Our mission is to deliver unforgettable, safe gaming experiences, and we look forward to seeing you in your favorite worlds,

The Ubisoft Team





 







 

 









 



 


